# Auto-orchestrator (decision tree)

Registry: `SYSTEM-REGISTRY.md`. Always-on: `00-agent-orchestrator.mdc`. Taxonomy: `SYSTEM-TAXONOMY.md` (on-demand).

## 1. Classify the task

```
User query
  ├─ Session / project memory              → user-memory MCP via parent agent
  ├─ Taxonomy / hub refresh / new skill    → SYSTEM-TAXONOMY.md + foundation-refresh
  ├─ Notion pages / T3 cleanup              → notion-workspace skill + user-notion MCP
  ├─ Video / storyboard / LVM               → production-studio skill
  ├─ Remotion / video-as-code / композиция  → remotion-code (plugin SECONDARY)
  ├─ shadcn blocks / docs for libs          → design-stack skill + context7 + @21st-dev/magic
  ├─ Repo patterns (vibe, swarm, visual)    → docs/knowledge-base/P2-REPOS.md
  ├─ Multi-agent analysis                    → up to 3 ephemeral specialists; no nested spawn
  ├─ Google mail/drive/calendar/GSC       → google-workspace MCP (OAuth on reload) · gsc-audit.ps1 CSV
  ├─ Maps / geo MCP                       → google-maps endpoint · gemini fallback
  ├─ Grill / согласовать план / большая задача → grill-rounds (route clarify-first)
  ├─ New project / с нуля / wayfinder         → wayfinder then WBS (route from-scratch)
  ├─ Client glossary / CONTEXT.md             → project-context (never in hub)
  ├─ Mega-task / WBS / эпики / декомпозиция → task-decomposition (Plan, then Boss yes)
  ├─ Refactor / review / surgical edit     → karpathy-guidelines.mdc + gitnexus if symbols
  ├─ Supply-chain / extension inventory    → bumblebee scan → cybersecurity
  ├─ Prompt templates library              → prompts.chat MCP (if configured)
  ├─ Marketing/sales/design persona        → agency-agents skill + @slug in rules/agency/
  ├─ Squad visual monitor                  → pixel-office.ps1 (opt-in)
  ├─ Single URL content                      → user-fetch (or Exa fetch if blocked)
  ├─ Web research / fact-check / docs        → plugin-exa-exa (ONE provider)
  ├─ Live page / form / E2E UI               → cursor-ide-browser
  ├─ Scale crawl / Actors / anti-bot         → Apify (APIFY-POLICY — ok when best tool; confirm if >$1)
  ├─ Clone / rebuild website                 → clone-website skill + browser
  ├─ HTML prototype / motion / deck          → open-design skill (@huashu = legacy alias)
  ├─ 21st.dev / shadcn registry UI           → 21st-design + @21st-dev/magic
  ├─ SEO / GEO audit                         → seo-geo skill pack
  ├─ Dev OS / bootstrap / research-first     → dev-os skill; research sprints → dev-os-research agent
  ├─ Project execution (build/QA/ship)       → domain skill + ephemeral build/review/QA roles
  ├─ Security audit                          → cybersecurity skill
  ├─ Symbol edit in indexed repo             → gitnexus impact → edit → detect_changes
  ├─ CI / PR checks failing                  → fix-ci / ci-investigator / shell
  ├─ Broad "how does X work" in repo         → explore subagent OR gitnexus_query
  ├─ Deploy / Vercel                         → plugin-vercel-vercel + deployment-expert
  ├─ Supabase / DB                           → plugin-supabase-supabase
  └─ Stripe / Clerk / Figma / Zapier         → matching plugin MCP + plugin skill
```

## 2. Load minimal context

1. One matching **rule** (if not already always-on)
2. One **SKILL.md** if triggers match
3. One **MCP descriptor JSON** before first tool call on that server
4. **Subagent** only if steps are independent or scope is large

## 2.1 Semantic preflight

The hook emits `stage`, confidence and `REQUIRED` actions. Treat them as a
state machine, not suggestions:

```
social → no-op
clear-small → matched skill/tool
ambiguous → route-advisor once
decisions → grill-rounds
research → current external evidence
tradeoff → LLM Council
systemic → options + architecture + WBS
high-risk → confirmation before action
```

The user does not need to name a skill. Simple action/object/context language is
enough. Execute each applicable required stage or report a concrete blocker.
Maximum three ephemeral agents; never restore Project Squad automatically.

## 3. After substantive work

- **Memory:** contextual read via `user-memory`; propose durable write to Boss
  before mutating memory. Project Squad/squad-memory remain archived.
- **Git commit:** `detect_changes()` if hub code symbols changed
- **Aikido:** scan first-party source changes before completion
- **Receipt:** report only systems actually used and what evidence they added

